```file:/runs/kit/REQ-011/ci/INTEGRITY_EVAL.json
{
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "req_id": "REQ-011",
  "verdict": "salvageable",
  "summary": "The candidate is a real UI implementation, not a placeholder: it includes typed DTOs, runtime URL resolution, TanStack Query fetch/mutation logic, a substantial inbox screen, and supporting tests. It covers the main REQ-011 behaviors at component level. However, it is not yet hardening-ready because promotion fit is only partial, the backend contract is assumed rather than evidenced from dependency outputs, test depth is limited for negative and refresh-path behavior, and docs/CI overstate deploy-target smoke portability that the emitted Playwright spec does not actually support.",
  "scope_fidelity": {
    "status": "partial",
    "notes": [
      "The emitted UI covers the declared REQ-011 behaviors: open task listing, workflow state badges for the five backend states, direct detail navigation, conditional retry affordance, and client-side read/refresh behavior.",
      "Operator-facing labels are in Italian and the page is localized consistently with slice-1 expectations.",
      "The detail navigation target and inbox/read endpoints are assumptions documented in README/KIT, not verified against emitted dependency artifacts for REQ-007 and REQ-010.",
      "Acceptance says users can open document detail directly from a task row; the implementation provides explicit links/buttons rather than row-level interaction. This is likely acceptable functionally but narrower than the wording suggests."
    ]
  },
  "source_substance": {
    "status": "adequate",
    "notes": [
      "Source implementation has real mass for a frontend UI REQ: types, runtime adapter, query/mutation hook, substantial React screen/view, and page entrypoint.",
      "Workflow badge mapping, read-state mutation, optimistic update, conditional retry visibility, and error-state rendering are implemented in source rather than described only in docs.",
      "The implementation is still self-contained and somewhat ad hoc: it uses direct fetch calls and local UI primitives instead of showing alignment with the planned shared frontend query/UI module families.",
      "No obvious placeholder seams or empty wrappers are present, so this is not skeletal."
    ]
  },
  "test_substance": {
    "status": "partial",
    "notes": [
      "Tests exercise real behavior: runtime URL normalization, list rendering, detail links, retry visibility, read-state mutation, refresh action, and a 401 state.",
      "Coverage is still narrow relative to the docs and promotion expectations: there is no explicit 403 test, no generic remote error test, no empty-state test, no detail-disabled case, and no evidence that all five workflow badges are asserted.",
      "The 'without full page reload' claim is only indirectly tested through mocked fetch/update behavior; there is no stronger browser-level assertion around client-side navigation/update semantics.",
      "The Playwright smoke is useful locally but is minimal and validates only a mocked same-origin path."
    ]
  },
  "docs_code_coherence": {
    "status": "mixed",
    "notes": [
      "README, KIT, HOWTO, and LTC generally match the emitted files, runtime env vars, and main commands.",
      "The docs correctly state that the inbox/read backend contract is assumed and that retry execution itself is out of scope.",
      "There is a material mismatch around deploy-target smoke: docs and LTC imply the same Playwright smoke can be pointed at AWS/UAT, but the emitted smoke spec only intercepts '**/api-mock/**' routes and is therefore clearly tailored to the local mocked profile.",
      "The docs rely on repository-provided QueryClientProvider, Next.js setup, and toolchain wiring that are not emitted here; that is acceptable as an assumption, but it weakens the self-contained operational contract."
    ]
  },
  "promotion_fit": {
    "status": "partial",
    "notes": [
      "Module placement under `frontend/app/workflow/inbox` is consistent with the planned namespace and should promote into canonical `src/` with low file-move risk.",
      "Tests are localized and reviewable, which is good for staged promotion.",
      "Promotion fit is weakened because the candidate does not demonstrate use of the planned shared frontend query/UI families and instead hardcodes its own fetch/query surface locally.",
      "The implementation also hardcodes document-detail route construction and an assumed inbox/read REST contract without showing reconciliation with canonical shared routing or API clients."
    ]
  },
  "shared_common_assessment": {
    "status": "mixed",
    "notes": [
      "The candidate does not introduce unnecessary new shared/common modules, which avoids premature extraction.",
      "However, PLAN explicitly points REQ-011 toward `frontend.app.shared.query` and `frontend.app.shared.ui`; this candidate bypasses that intended reuse entirely.",
      "This is not an architectural violation severe enough to reject the slice, but it is a promotion concern because later consolidation work is still needed."
    ]
  },
  "dual_mode_assessment": {
    "status": "acceptable",
    "notes": [
      "Dual-mode integrity is conceptually sound: local and aws modes preserve the same business behavior and differ only through runtime configuration.",
      "The source keeps one UI architecture and one DTO shape across profiles; local mode does not replace the promotable design with a separate fake implementation.",
      "The `profile` flag itself is lightly used and most behavior depends only on `NEXT_PUBLIC_API_BASE_URL`, but this is still an adapter/config approach rather than a divergent architecture."
    ]
  },
  "blockers": [
    "Playwright smoke and docs/CI contract are misaligned: the emitted smoke spec is local `/api-mock` oriented but documentation presents it as deploy-target portable.",
    "Promotion alignment to planned shared frontend query/UI module families is not demonstrated.",
    "Backend contract dependencies for `/tasks/inbox`, `/tasks/{taskId}/read`, and `/validation/workspace/{documentId}` are assumed rather than evidenced against dependent REQ outputs.",
    "Test coverage is too shallow to credibly harden error handling and edge-state behavior for promotion."
  ],
  "hardening_targets": [
    "Align smoke documentation and LTC with the actual Playwright harness, or constrain the documented smoke scope explicitly to the local mocked profile.",
    "Add tests for 403, generic remote error, empty inbox, disabled detail access, and full badge/state coverage across all five workflow states.",
    "Strengthen promotion fit by reconciling the inbox fetch/query/UI layer with the planned shared frontend module families instead of keeping a fully local ad hoc client surface.",
    "Validate or explicitly contract-test the assumed inbox/read endpoints and detail-route integration against the dependent REQ interfaces before promotion hardening.",
    "Tighten navigation/read-state behavior around detail open so the mark-as-read path is not merely fire-and-forget when the user leaves the page."
  ]
}
```
